     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 8pt;line-height:107%;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\">Hi <span style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\">Phil and members</span>,</p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 8pt;line-height:107%;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">I’m doing a\r\nsimulation study for unidimensional vertical equating, with:</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 8pt;line-height:107%;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">1) 5 groups\r\nand 96 items (3PL). Each group (with 10000 individuals) answers to 24 items. Group means\r\n0,1,2,3,4 and sd 1, 0.8, 0.9, 1.1, 1.2</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 8pt;line-height:107%;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">2) There are\r\n6 common items between adjacent groups (k and k+1).</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 8pt;line-height:107%;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">3) Data U has\r\nNA to non answered items.</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 8pt;line-height:107%;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"> </span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 8pt;line-height:107%;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">I’ve tried:</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 8pt;line-height:107%;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">group= paste0(&quot;G&quot;,rep(1:5,\r\neach=10000))</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 8pt;line-height:107%;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">multipleGroup(U,\r\n1, itemtype = &#39;3PL&#39;, group = group, <a name=\"m_-4945726801515705301_OLE_LINK3\" rel=\"nofollow\"></a><a name=\"m_-4945726801515705301_OLE_LINK2\" rel=\"nofollow\"></a><a name=\"m_-4945726801515705301_OLE_LINK1\" rel=\"nofollow\">invariance=c(&#39;slopes&#39;, &#39;intercepts&#39;, &#39;free_var&#39;,&#39;free_means&#39;)</a>,\r\ntechnical = list(NCYCLES = 1000))</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 8pt;line-height:107%;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">and with</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 8pt;line-height:107%;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">invariance=c(<a name=\"m_-4945726801515705301_OLE_LINK7\" rel=\"nofollow\">colnames(U),</a>&#39;slopes&#39;, <a name=\"m_-4945726801515705301_OLE_LINK6\" rel=\"nofollow\"></a><a name=\"m_-4945726801515705301_OLE_LINK5\" rel=\"nofollow\"></a><a name=\"m_-4945726801515705301_OLE_LINK4\" rel=\"nofollow\">&#39;</a>intercepts&#39;,\r\n&#39;free_var&#39;,&#39;free_means&#39;)</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 8pt;line-height:107%;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"> </span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 8pt;line-height:107%;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">The results\r\nare not fine for parameter recovery. Without <a name=\"m_-4945726801515705301_OLE_LINK10\" rel=\"nofollow\"></a><a name=\"m_-4945726801515705301_OLE_LINK9\" rel=\"nofollow\"></a><a name=\"m_-4945726801515705301_OLE_LINK8\" rel=\"nofollow\">colnames(U) </a>the “c”\r\nparameters are different for each group, “a” and “b” are equals over the 5\r\ngroups, good estimates. Good abilities estimates too. But with colnames(U) all\r\nthe parameters estimates are the same <a name=\"m_-4945726801515705301_OLE_LINK11\" rel=\"nofollow\">for the 5 groups</a>,\r\nbad estimates.</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 8pt;line-height:107%;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">What I am\r\ndoing wrong? Do you have any good “suggestion”?</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 8pt;line-height:107%;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"><br></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 8pt;line-height:107%;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">Thanks in advance,</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 8pt;line-height:107%;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">Heliton Tavares</span></p></div>\r\n"
    ]
